Task: Migrate dashboard-summary-controller.ts (reopened) — fix legacy raw SQL

Summary:
Replaced legacy Prisma quoted PascalCase identifiers ("UserActivity",
"XPLogs", "createdAt") and the singular legacy table 'article' with
the unified Drizzle/Postgres snake_case names (user_activity, xp_logs,
created_at, articles). Switched from the executeBatchRawQueries helper
(which previously did unsafe $n string interpolation) to direct
db.execute(sql`...`) calls so each period boundary is bound as a
parameter by Drizzle/postgres-js.

Files:
- apps/reading-advantage/server/controllers/dashboard-summary-controller.ts
- apps/reading-advantage/__test__/dashboard-summary-controller.test.ts (new)

Why:
The 2026-05-23 review found the dashboard summary endpoint would fail
at runtime against the unified schema because it still referenced
Prisma's pre-unification quoted PascalCase tables and columns. Direct
parameterized sql template usage eliminates both the schema-name bug
and the SQL injection surface in one change.
